            <ArticleTitle>Multilobed cystic dilation of the ventriculus terminalis (CDVT).</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2013-008654</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2013008654</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The cystic dilation of ventriculus terminalis (CDVT) is a rare anatomical variant in adulthood. In this report we describe a new case of an adult with multilobed CDVT, causing low-back pain and subjective disturbances in walking. A myelotomy with fenestration of the cyst was performed with a good clinical and radiological outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
